@startuml
title OCI Data Integration – Task Reconciliation Sequence

participant Client
participant "Orchestration Engine\n(Control Plane)" as Orch
participant "Task State Store" as Store
participant "Execution Engine\n(DB / Spark / External)" as Exec
participant "Reconciliation Loop" as Recon

== Task Submission ==
Client -> Orch: Trigger Pipeline Run
Orch -> Store: Create Task (CREATED)
Orch -> Store: Update Task (SCHEDULED)

== Task Execution ==
Orch -> Exec: Start Task Execution
Orch -> Store: Update Task (RUNNING)

== Normal Completion ==
Exec -> Orch: Task Completed
Orch -> Store: Update Task (COMPLETED)
Orch -> Orch: Schedule Downstream Tasks

== Failure Scenario: Callback Lost ==
Exec -> Exec: Task Completes Successfully
note right of Exec: Callback fails / network issue

Recon -> Store: Scan RUNNING tasks
Recon -> Exec: Query execution status
Exec --> Recon: COMPLETED
Recon -> Store: Update Task (COMPLETED)
Recon -> Orch: Resume DAG execution

== Failure Scenario: Execution Failure ==
Exec -> Exec: Task Fails
note right of Exec: No immediate callback

Recon -> Store: Detect stale RUNNING task
Recon -> Exec: Query execution status
Exec --> Recon: FAILED
Recon -> Store: Update Task (FAILED)

alt Retry Available
    Recon -> Store: Update Task (RETRYING)
    Recon -> Orch: Trigger Retry
else Retries Exhausted
    Recon -> Store: Update Task (ABORTED)
end

== Orchestrator Crash Recovery ==
note over Orch: Orchestrator restarts
Recon -> Store: Load RUNNING tasks
Recon -> Exec: Reconcile execution state
Recon -> Store: Correct task state
Recon -> Orch: Resume pipeline execution
@enduml